---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology — Is Poland Safe Now?"
  description="How Is Poland Safe Now? classifies regional security status using TypeSafe AI, and the limits of the current pipeline."
  path="/methodology"
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-6 px-4 py-8 text-slate-700">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Methodology</h1>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Current phase: live, AI-assisted classification</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Every region's status is produced by <code>TypeSafeAiClassificationService</code>, which calls TypeSafe
        AI's System One API once per request to classify each of the 16 voivodeships. There is no dedicated
        news-collection pipeline yet (see <a class="underline" href="/about">About</a>), so classifications reflect
        the model's own knowledge as of the request rather than a stored, citable evidence trail. If the TypeSafe
        AI call is unavailable, misconfigured, or returns something unusable, affected regions show
        <strong>Unknown</strong> — never a false Green.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Status levels</h2>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Green</strong> — no elevated regional signal found.</li>
        <li><strong>Yellow</strong> — elevated situation requiring attention.</li>
        <li><strong>Red</strong> — serious active warning or confirmed incident.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Unknown</strong> — missing, stale, conflicting, or insufficient information. Missing data always
          resolves to Unknown, never Green.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Planned pipeline (not yet implemented)</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        A future phase will collect news from public sources relevant to Poland's security situation (the
        Russia-Ukraine war, Belarus border activity, Kaliningrad, airspace violations, drone or missile incidents,
        RCB warnings, and transport disruptions) and pass that evidence to TypeSafe AI alongside each question, so
        classifications are backed by citable sources rather than the model's own knowledge alone. Classifications
        will also run on a schedule and be stored with full evidence trails in the database, following the same
        <code>ClassificationService</code> interface this phase already defines.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Map data</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Voivodeship boundaries are sourced from Poland's official geospatial registry (GUGiK PRG) and converted to a
        local SVG at development time — see
        <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/pvgomes/ispolandsafenow/blob/main/DATA_SOURCES.md">
          DATA_SOURCES.md
        </a>
        in the repository for the full attribution and license.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Limits</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        This is an independent information service, not an official warning system, and cannot guarantee safety.
        Always follow instructions from Polish authorities and RCB. For emergencies, call 112.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
